  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "When running the latest release using `git clone --recursive https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet.git` on a fresh Raspberry Pi OS install, after installing the dependencies and running `setup_env.py`, it fails to compile. \n\nThe error was caused by the missing headers at `ggml-bitnet-lut.cpp` and `ggml-bitnet-mad.cpp`, located at src/ directory\n\nAdding the following code to the beginning of both files solved the problem\n\n`#include <stdlib.h>`\n`#include <string.h>`\n\nI don`t know if it`s a architecture related problem, or it the code wasn`t prepared to be build on POSIX systems, but this little modification solved the problem to me. \nHope it helps other users facing the same problem!",
  "closed_at": "2024-10-21T08:39:08Z",
